Caveat
======

GraphicalModels requires Graphs.m2 and StatGraphs.m2. These packages allow the
user to create graphs whose vertices are labeled arbitrarily. However, several
functions in GraphicalModels sort the vertices of the graph. Hence, graphs used
as input to methods in GraphicalModels must have sortable vertex labels, e.g.,
all numbers or all letters.

The methods in GraphicalModels differ in the classes of acceptable graphs for
input:

- functions used in package GraphicalModelsMLE (*note gaussianRing:
gaussianRing,, *note covarianceMatrix: covarianceMatrix,,  *note
bidirectedEdgesMatrix: bidirectedEdgesMatrix,, *note directedEdgesMatrix:
directedEdgesMatrix,, *note directedEdgesMatrix: directedEdgesMatrix,, *note
undirectedEdgesMatrix: undirectedEdgesMatrix,) and *note
conditionalIndependenceIdeal: conditionalIndependenceIdeal, accept *note Graph:
(Graphs)Graph,, *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,, *note Bigraph:
(StatGraphs)Bigraph, and *note MixedGraph: (StatGraphs)MixedGraph,.

- conditional independence statement generators (*note pairMarkov: pairMarkov,,
*note localMarkov: localMarkov, and *note globalMarkov: globalMarkov,) accept
only *note Graph: (Graphs)Graph, or *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,;

- the remaining functions that accepts graphs, only accept *note Graph:
(Graphs)Graph,, *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph, or *note MixedGraph:
(StatGraphs)MixedGraph, without undirected edges.





