covarianceMatrix -- covariance matrix of a Gaussian graphical model
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        covarianceMatrix R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, which should be a gaussianRing
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the $n \times{} n$ covariance
        matrix of the Gaussian graphical model.

Description
===========

This method returns the $n \times{} n$ covariance matrix of the Gaussian
graphical model where $n$ is the number of random variables in the model.  If
the gaussianRing was created using a graph, $n$ will be the number of vertices
of the graph. If this function is called without a graph $G$, it is assumed
that $R$ is the gaussianRing of a directed acyclic graph.



