File: GraphicalModels.info, Node: gaussianParametrization_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSimpleTreks=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Next: gaussianRing, Prev: gaussianParametrization, Up: Top

gaussianParametrization(...,SimpleTreks=>...) -- optional input for gaussianParametrization
*******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = gaussianParametrization(R,SimpleTreks => true)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, which should be a gaussianRing
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the parametrization of the
        covariance matrix in terms of treks

Description
===========

Put SimpleTreks => true as an argument in the function *note
gaussianParametrization: gaussianParametrization, to compute a parametrization
of the covariance matrix $S=(s_{(i,j)})$ where $s_{(i,j)}$ is the sum of
monomials corresponding to simple treks between vertices $i$ and $j$. Here, a
simple trek is a trek $(P_L,P_R)$ where the paths $P_L$ and $P_R$ do not have
any common vertices except perhaps at their source. See *note trekSeparation:
trekSeparation, for the definition of a trek.

If the option SimpleTreks => false is used, then the sum is over all treks, and
not just simple treks.



See also
========

  * *note gaussianParametrization: gaussianParametrization, -- parametrization
    of the covariance matrix in terms of treks

Functions with optional argument named SimpleTreks:
===================================================

  * *note gaussianParametrization(...,SimpleTreks=>...):
    gaussianParametrization_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSimpleTreks=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, --
    optional input for gaussianParametrization

Further information
===================

  * Default value: *note false: (Macaulay2Doc)false,
  * Function: *note gaussianParametrization: gaussianParametrization, --
    parametrization of the covariance matrix in terms of treks
  * Option key: *note SimpleTreks: SimpleTreks, -- optional input for
    gaussianParametrization
