        pd_rp, => ..., default value "l", symbol used for indeterminates in a
        ring of Gaussian joint probability distributions
      * *note pVariableName: gaussianRing_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmpVariableName=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value "p", symbol used for indeterminates in a
        ring of Gaussian joint probability distributions
      * *note sVariableName: gaussianRing_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmsVariableName=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value "s", symbol used for indeterminates in a
        ring of Gaussian joint probability distributions
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a polynomial ring with
        indeterminates associated to the graphical model

Description
===========

This function creates a ring whose indeterminates are the covariances of an n
dimensional Gaussian random vector.  Using a graph, digraph, or mixed graph $G$
as input gives a gaussianRing with extra indeterminates related to the
parametrization of the graphical model associated to that graph. Check the
details of the gaussianRing for each type of input:

* *note gaussianRing(ZZ): gaussianRing_lpZZ_rp,

* *note gaussianRing(Graph): gaussianRing_lpGraph_rp,

* *note gaussianRing(Digraph): gaussianRing_lpDigraph_rp,

* *note gaussianRing(Bigraph): gaussianRing_lpBigraph_rp,

* *note gaussianRing(MixedGraph): gaussianRing_lpMixedGraph_rp,

The indeterminates of the ring - $s_{(i,j)},k_{(i,j)},l_{(i,j)},p_{(i,j)}$ -
can be placed into an appropriate matrix format using the functions *note
covarianceMatrix: covarianceMatrix,, *note undirectedEdgesMatrix:
undirectedEdgesMatrix,, *note directedEdgesMatrix: directedEdgesMatrix,, and
*note bidirectedEdgesMatrix: bidirectedEdgesMatrix, respectively.

The variable names that appear can be changed using the options sVariableName,
lVariableName, pVariableName, and kVariableName



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = mixedGraph(digraph {{b,{c,d}},{c,{d}}},bigraph {{a,d}})             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = MixedGraph{Bigraph => Bigraph{a => {d}}   }                             |
|                                   d => {a}                                  |
|                Digraph => Digraph{b => {c, d}}                              |
|                                   c => {d}                                  |
|                                   d => {}                                   |
|                Graph => Graph{}                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : MixedGraph                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = gaussianRing (G,pVariableName => psi)                               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : gens R                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {l   , l   , l   , psi   , psi   , psi   , psi   , psi   , s   , s   ,  |
|       b,c   b,d   c,d     a,a     b,b     c,c     d,d     a,d   a,a   a,b   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   , s   }                         |
|      a,c   a,d   b,b   b,c   b,d   c,c   c,d   d,d                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The routines  *note conditionalIndependenceIdeal:
conditionalIndependenceIdeal,, *note trekIdeal: trekIdeal,, *note
covarianceMatrix: covarianceMatrix,, *note undirectedEdgesMatrix:
undirectedEdgesMatrix,, *note directedEdgesMatrix: directedEdgesMatrix,, *note
bidirectedEdgesMatrix: bidirectedEdgesMatrix,, *note gaussianVanishingIdeal:
gaussianVanishingIdeal, and *note gaussianParametrization:
gaussianParametrization, require that the ring be created by this function.



