        gaussianRing,  using a graphs of classes *note Graph: (Graphs)Graph,,
        *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph, or  *note MixedGraph:
        (StatGraphs)MixedGraph, without undirected edges as input.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note OldVersion: gaussianVanishingIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOldVersion=>_pd_
        pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value false, optional argument in
        gaussianVanishingIdeal to use old method for gaussianRings coming from
        directed graphs
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, ideal in R

Description
===========

gaussianVanishingIdeal computes the ideal in $R$ of homogeneous polynomial
relations on the variance-covariance parameters of a graphical model on $G$ as
explained in Chapter 3.3 of ``Lectures on Algebraic Statistics'' by Drton,
Sturmfels, and Sullivant.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{a,b},{b,c},{c,d},{a,d}})                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = Graph{a => {b, d}}                                                      |
|           b => {a, c}                                                       |
|           c => {b, d}                                                       |
|           d => {a, c}                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Graph                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = gaussianRing G                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = gaussianVanishingIdeal(R);                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ideal mingens J / print;                                                |
|                    2                                                        |
|s   s   s    - s   s    - s   s   s    + s   s   s    + s   s   s    -       |
| a,d b,c b,d    a,c b,d    a,d b,b c,d    a,b b,d c,d    a,c b,b d,d         |
|                2                                                            |
|s   s   s    - s   s    - s   s   s    + s   s   s    + s   s   s    -       |
| a,c a,d b,c    a,c b,d    a,b a,d c,c    a,a b,d c,c    a,b a,c c,d         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|s   s   s                                                                    |
| a,b b,c d,d                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|s   s   s                                                                    |
| a,a b,c c,d                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This method works for graphs, digraphs and mixed graphs without undirected
edges.



+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : G = digraph {{a,{b,c}}, {b,{c,d}}, {c,{}}, {d,{}}}                   |
|                                                                          |
|o5 = Digraph{a => {c, b}}                                                 |
|             b => {c, d}                                                  |
|             c => {}                                                      |
|             d => {}                                                      |
|                                                                          |
|o5 : Digraph                                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = gaussianRing G                                                   |
|                                                                          |
|o6 = R                                                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o6 : PolynomialRing                                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : gaussianVanishingIdeal(R)                                            |
|                                                                          |
|o7 = ideal (s   s    - s   s   , s   s    - s   s   , s   s    - s   s   )|
|             b,c b,d    b,b c,d   a,d b,c    a,b c,d   a,d b,b    a,b b,d |
|                                                                          |
|o7 : Ideal of R                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : H = mixedGraph(digraph {{a,{c}},{b,{c}}, {c,{d}}},bigraph {{c,d}})   |
|                                                                          |
|o8 = MixedGraph{Bigraph => Bigraph{c => {d}}}                             |
|                                   d => {c}                               |
|                Digraph => Digraph{a => {c}}                              |
|                                   b => {c}                               |
|                                   c => {d}                               |
|                                   d => {}                                |
|                Graph => Graph{}                                          |
|                                                                          |
|o8 : MixedGraph                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : S = gaussianRing H                                                   |
|                                                                          |
|o9 = S                                                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o9 : PolynomialRing                                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : gaussianVanishingIdeal(S)                                           |
|                                                                          |
|o10 = ideal (s   , s   s    - s   s   )                                   |
|              a,b   a,d b,c    a,c b,d                                    |
|                                                                          |
|o10 : Ideal of S                                                          |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This method currently works on really small examples because it computes the
vanishing ideal as an elimination ideal.

See also
========

  * *note gaussianRing: gaussianRing, -- ring of Gaussian correlations on n
    random variables or a graphical model
  * *note trekIdeal: trekIdeal, -- trek separation ideal of a mixed graph
  * *note OldVersion: OldVersion, -- optional argument in
    gaussianVanishingIdeal to use old method for gaussianRings coming from
    directed graphs

Ways to use gaussianVanishingIdeal:
===================================

  * "gaussianVanishingIdeal(Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

