gaussianVanishingIdeal(...,OldVersion=>...) -- optional argument in gaussianVanishingIdeal to use old method for gaussianRings coming from directed graphs
**********************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        gaussianVanishingIdeal(R,G,OldVersion=>false)
  * Inputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, false by default

Description
===========

By default, *note gaussianVanishingIdeal: gaussianVanishingIdeal, uses the code
of the current version. However, if the graph only has directed edges, the user
can choose to use the code from the previous version which is based on (2) from
Seth Sullivant, Kelli Talaska, and Jan Draisma, Trek separation for Gaussian
graphical models, The Annals of Statistics 38.3 (2010): 1665-1685.



