This linear transformation simplifies ideals and/or polynomials involving $
p_{u_1,u_2,..., +,...,u_n} $. Sometimes, the resulting ideals are toric ideals
as the example below shows. For more details see the paper "Algebraic Geometry
of Bayesian Networks" by Garcia, Stillman, and Sturmfels.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G = digraph  {{1,{}},{2,{1}},{3,{1}},{4,{2,3}}}                         |
