File: GraphicalModels.info, Node: markovRing_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficients=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Next: markovRing_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariableName=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, Prev: markovRing, Up: Top

markovRing(...,Coefficients=>...) -- optional input to choose the base field in markovRing or gaussianRing
**********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        gaussianRing(n,Coefficients=>Ring)
        gaussianRing(G,Coefficients=>Ring)
        markovRing(d,Coefficients=>Ring)
  * Inputs:
      * d, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, with positive integer
        entries $(d_1,\dots ,d_r)$
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of random variables
      * G, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, or a
        *note digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,, or an instance of the type *note
        MixedGraph: (StatGraphs)MixedGraph, with directed and bidirected edges
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

In both markovRing and gaussianRing, the default coefficient ring is QQ.
Putting Coefficients => r for a choice of ring(field) r as an argument in the
function *note markovRing: markovRing, or *note gaussianRing: gaussianRing,
creates a ring with the desired coefficient ring.



+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R2 = markovRing ((2,2),Coefficients=>CC);|
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : coefficientRing R2                       |
|                                              |
|o2 = CC                                       |
|       53                                     |
|                                              |
|o2 : ComplexField                             |
+----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note markovRing: markovRing, -- ring of joint probability distributions on
    several discrete random variables
  * *note gaussianRing: gaussianRing, -- ring of Gaussian correlations on n
    random variables or a graphical model

Functions with optional argument named Coefficients:
====================================================

  * "gaussianRing(...,Coefficients=>...)"
  * *note markovRing(...,Coefficients=>...):
    markovRing_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficients=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- optional input to
    choose the base field in markovRing or gaussianRing

Further information
===================

  * Default value: *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
  * Function: *note markovRing: markovRing, -- ring of joint probability
    distributions on several discrete random variables
  * Option key: *note Coefficients: Coefficients, -- optional input to choose
    the base field
