undirectedEdgesMatrix -- matrix corresponding to the edges of an undirected graph
*********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        undirectedEdgesMatrix(R)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, which should be created with
        *note gaussianRing: gaussianRing, created with a *note graph:
        (Graphs)Graph, or an instance of the type *note MixedGraph:
        (StatGraphs)MixedGraph,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the n x n symmetric
        concentration matrix of an undirected gaussian graphical model.

Description
===========

This symmetric matrix has entries $k_{(i,i)}$ along the diagonal and entry
$k_{(i,j)}$ in the $(i,j)$ position if there is an edge  between i and j, and a
zero otherwise. The documentation of *note gaussianRing: gaussianRing, further
describes the indeterminates $k_{(i,j)}$.



+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({{a,b},{b,c},{c,d},{a,d}})|
|                                         |
|o1 = Graph{a => {b, d}}                  |
|           b => {a, c}                   |
|           c => {b, d}                   |
|           d => {a, c}                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : Graph                               |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = gaussianRing G                  |
|                                         |
|o2 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                      |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : compactMatrixForm =false;           |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = undirectedEdgesMatrix(R)        |
|                                         |
|o4 = |  k     k       0   k     |        |
|     |   a,a   a,b         a,d  |        |
|     |                          |        |
|     |  k     k     k       0   |        |
|     |   a,b   b,b   b,c        |        |
|     |                          |        |
|     |    0   k     k     k     |        |
|     |         b,c   c,c   c,d  |        |
|     |                          |        |
|     |  k       0   k     k     |        |
|     |   a,d         c,d   d,d  |        |
|                                         |
|             4      4                    |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                     |
+-----------------------------------------+

For mixed graphs with other types of edges, the size of the matrix coincides
with the number of elements in *note compU: compU,, which depends on the vertex
partition built in *note partitionLMG: (StatGraphs)partitionLMG,.



+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : G = mixedGraph(digraph {{1,3},{2,4}},bigraph {{3,4}},graph {{1,2}});|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = gaussianRing G;                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : K = undirectedEdgesMatrix(R)                                        |
|                                                                         |
|o7 = |  k     k     |                                                    |
|     |   1,1   1,2  |                                                    |
|     |              |                                                    |
|     |  k     k     |                                                    |
|     |   1,2   2,2  |                                                    |
|                                                                         |
|             2      2                                                    |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

